  <mods:abstract>Preparatory design for stained glass window at the chapel of Saint Mary?s Dominican convent in Dun Laoghaire, Co. Dublin. Saint Catherine of Siena holding lilies and encircled by roses; crown of thorns and lantern at base.
    Inscriptions: Design notes on right hand side, supplied by Prioress Sister M. Ignatius: ?separate tints. 1-head covering and wimple white linen. 2- Scapular cream. 3-undergarment. Hand turned up a little (not so dead like as in sketch. Sleeve same colour as undergarment. Scapular longer (down to x). Lantern bigger as in Father Heuston sketch. Crown disappears behind lantern.Signature: Bottom right corner: Clarke Studios, Dublin.

    Related to: See IE TCD MS 6056, folio 943 (order no 2363)</mods:abstract>
